        en: "Improving the clarity of games allows players to spend more of their mental effort on strategic planning rather than the mundane bookkeeping of calculating legal moves. This article discusses techniques for achieving this, by making the design do the work rather than the player, and demonstrates this concept through example. Such techniques include visual design, simplifying rules, clarifying rules, harnessing emergent strategies, and minimising mental bookkeeping.",
