        en: "This issue’s game design pattern deals with the notion of making the design do the work rather than the player. The aim is to free the player from the mundane bookkeeping of move-making, so that they can focus on the more interesting task of deciding which moves to make. This paper outlines relevant principles, then demonstrates these in relation to numerous examples and counterexamples from well-known – and some lesser-known – games and puzzles.",
